      ],
      "notes": "Start: hold the 90 x 90 x 8 mm hardwood blank with the two example 02 toe clamps on the left and right side midpoints, toes 5 mm onto the blank, 8 mm packing under their outer ends.\nOperation 1 drills 4 screw holes, 4 mm through, one in each corner of the frame, 8 mm in from both edges.\nThen the program retracts and stops at the operator stop (and parks there when the machine has an Operator stop park): Drive 4 screws, remove the 2 clamps, then press Cycle Start. Use 4 mm wood screws (head 8 mm or less) into the spoilboard.\nThe relief is cut next, and the outline last with 4 triangular tabs that leave bridges about 5 mm wide and 1.5 mm high, so the disc stays joined to the screwed-down frame.\nAfter the program: cut the 4 tabs, sand the stubs, then unscrew the frame.",
      "holdingMethod": "screws",
      "machineActions": [
        {
          "id": "915c7be8-f960-41ee-9e39-fadb2bdcd365",
          "kind": "operator_stop",
          "name": "Operator stop",
          "enabled": true,
          "afterOpId": "62d971b1-e599-4e66-a66d-ee0d5c45c0ee",
          "message": "Drive 4 screws, remove the 2 clamps, then press Cycle Start"
        }
      ]
    }
